; Provider-route executable family, 6 of 7 — one name, two sources.
;
; Both shaders yield `u_time`, from two *different* sources (so this is
; two extractions colliding, not one extraction counted twice). The
; second registration loses and reports `duplicate_cross_ref_target`,
; exactly as two `(phrase :name p0)` forms do on the identity route —
; the rule is about the registry, not about how names reach it.
;
; Worth stating because the neighbouring rule goes the other way: a name
; repeated *within* one source is the provider's business and is silently
; collapsed (a blob's internal redundancy is not a document error). Two
; sources in one scope claiming one name is the document's business,
; because the document chose to put both there.
;
; The reference resolves to the first declaration, so it contributes no
; diagnostic of its own — first-wins, as everywhere else.
(use-plugin "lines")

(shader :name a :src "u_time\nu_a")
(shader :name b :src "u_time\nu_b")

(bind :uniform u_time)
